{
 "about": "The process sweep's coverage: one entry per carrier, that is every file that starts a program under packs/ or tool-library/ (outside tests/): the 62 copies of the shared PROCESS block (# BEGIN SHARED PROCESS), the files that start a program by their own code, and the shell recipes. tests/process-sweep-coverage.test.ts holds this file to the code and fails on a carrier it does not list. Classes: held (reports files a program wrote, or that the tool hashes or reports; must call process_apply or the named tool-local equivalent in `apply`, and is at most partial where the absence of a leftover cannot be proven), pipe-only (reports what a program printed on a pipe; partial for an ended leftover or a cut pipe, not held to the unproven rule), no-program (starts no program), local-mechanism (its own mechanism, named in `mechanism`; `marker` is a line of the code that shows it), twin (byte copy of `pack_file`). `tests` lists the suites with a real abandoned child for the carrier; `known_gap` says why a carrier has none. `pipe_cut_gap` names a tool that reads a pipe through the block and leaves the status alone when the pipe is cut; `cut_through` names the function that puts the cut into its reasons. `apply` is process_apply, or the local function that does its job (program_group_problems, or process_verdict read in the tool itself). The first classification came from the process-sweep audit (section 2) and the verification verdicts of packages P0 to P7; `source` names the committed fragment that states the class.",
 "classified_at": "5c02ca81",
